  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1116 AM CST Tue Nov 17 2026\n\nSurface high pressure centered over the east central U.S. will \nproduce southerly winds across our region the rest of the week. \nThis will result in a warming trend, with both high and low \ntemperatures by Friday through Saturday night around 10 degrees \nabove normal in the middle 60s to around 70 degrees, and the \nmiddle 40s to around 50 degrees.\n\nA cold front will move through the middle Mississippi and lower\nOhio valleys Sunday. Ahead of the front, 15-25% chances of light\nshowers will spread across the northwest half of the PAH\nforecast area late Saturday night, with 15% chances lingering \ninto Sunday mainly east of the Mississippi River. With lacking\nmoisture and the fairly isolated nature of showers, rainfall\namounts will generally be a couple of hundredths of an inch or\nless, with many areas remaining dry.\n\nBehind the front, northwest winds will gradually bring in colder\nair, and temperatures by Monday night into Tuesday will be a \nfew degrees below normal with lows the upper 20s to lower 30s\nand highs of 50 to 55 degrees.",
